{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Remember.</b> זָכוֹר and שָׁמוֹר were spoken in one utterance. And likewise ״מְחַלְלֶיהָ מוֹת יוּמָת״ (Exodus 31), ״וּבְיוֹם הַשַּׁבָּת שְׁנֵי כְבָשִׂים״ (Numbers 28); and likewise ״לֹא תִלְבַּשׁ שַׁעַטְנֵז, גְּדִלִים תַּעֲשֶׂה לָּךְ״ (Deuteronomy 22); and likewise ״עֶרְוַת אֵשֶׁת אָחִיךָ״ (Leviticus 18), ״יְבָמָהּ יָבֹא עָלֶיהָ״ (Deuteronomy 25). As it says: ״אַחַת דִּבֶּר אֱלֹהִים שְׁתַּיִם זוּ שָׁמָעְתִּי״ (Psalms 62). <b>Remember.</b> It is a paʿol form, like אָכוֹל וְשָׁתוֹ (Isaiah 22), הָלוֹךְ וּבָכֹה (II Samuel 3). And so its meaning: give heart to always remember the Sabbath day, so that if a fine item comes your way you shall set it aside for the Sabbath (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:19.566685821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}